# 🛡️ SafeGo: End-to-End UML Use Case Specification & Architecture Diagram

## 1. Executive Summary & UML Boundary Overview

**SafeGo** is an intelligent, safety-centric mobility and ride-hailing platform engineered around real-time telemetry, Scikit-Learn Machine Learning safety classifiers, dynamic pricing regression, live GPS route deviation detection, multi-modal emergency dispatching, and inclusive passenger safety policies.

### System Boundary
The **SafeGo Platform System Boundary** encapsulates all services, engines, and consoles:
- **Client Interfaces**: React 18 Single-Page Application (Rider Booking Console, Driver Portal, Admin Command Center, Safety Hub, Voice Assistant).
- **Backend Services**: Asynchronous FastAPI core engine, WebSocket Manager, Indian Cities Geocoding Engine, and Beanie ODM persistence.
- **Embedded AI & ML**: Dual Scikit-Learn inference engines (`SafetyPredictor` Random Forest Classifier & `FareSurgePredictor` Random Forest Regressor) and NLP Sentiment Analysis (`TextBlob`).
- **External Integration Services**: Twilio Emergency Voice & SMS Gateway, Cloudinary KYC storage, Photon/Nominatim OpenStreetMap geocoding, and National Emergency Services (112).

